We are excited to announce that the POPL edition of the Programming
Languages Mentoring Workshop (PLMW) is returning for its 15th installment
in Mexico City, Mexico!

PLMW is designed to help late-stage undergraduate and early-stage PhD
students interested in programming languages (PL) research connect with the
broader PL community.

The workshop includes:
- Technical sessions covering both foundational and cutting-edge PL
research topics
- Mentoring sessions on building a PL research career; covering topics such
as how to give a research talk and write a research paper, how to apply to
grad school, academic vs. industry research careers, and more
- Social sessions to connect with PL researchers and fellow students who
share your interests

If this sounds exciting to you, we warmly welcome your attendance! We
especially encourage women, underrepresented minorities, and people with
disabilities to attend. Note, attendance is open to everybody who is
registered for workshops for the day.

-------------------------------------------------
Call for Travel Scholarship Applications
-------------------------------------------------

Our sponsors have generously donated scholarship funds for qualified
students who do not have the funds to attend PLMW. These scholarships can
cover expenses (airfare, hotel, and registration fees) for attendance at
both the workshop and the POPL conference itself. Make sure to apply at the
link below by the application deadline for consideration.

*Scholarship application deadline*: October 19, 2026 (AoE)
*Apply here*:
https://popl27.sigplan.org/home/PLMW-POPL-2027#Call-for-Scholarship-Applications

We also strongly recommend applying for the POPL Student Research
Competition and student volunteering at POPL if possible.

We hope to see you in Mexico City!
The PLMW@POPL 2027 Organizing Committee

